<header><p class="st-kicker">other · North America and Oceania</p><h1 class="st-title">Provisional Government of Saskatchewan</h1><p class="st-meta">1885 CE – 1885 CE · capital Batoche</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The government declared by Louis Riel at Batoche in 1885, whose defeat ended the North-West Resistance and led to Riel's execution.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/metis">Métis</a> families who had moved west from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-river-colony">Red River</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-saskatchewan-river">South Saskatchewan River</a> after 1870 feared losing their river lots to surveys, while <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cree">Cree</a> nations faced hunger after the buffalo vanished. In 1884 they invited <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-riel">Louis Riel</a> back from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/montana">Montana</a>. When <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottawa">Ottawa</a> failed to respond to petitions, Riel proclaimed a provisional government at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/batoche">Batoche</a> in March 1885.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Its council was called the Exovedate, a name <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-riel">Riel</a> coined meaning 'from the flock', and it mixed politics with Riel's religious ideas. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gabriel-dumont">Gabriel Dumont</a> led its military. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/metis">Métis</a> fighters defeated the North-West Mounted Police at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-duck-lake">Duck Lake</a> on 26 March, while <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cree">Cree</a> warriors from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/big-bear">Big Bear's</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poundmaker">Poundmaker's</a> bands fought separately at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frog-lake-massacre">Frog Lake</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battleford">Battleford</a> and Cut Knife.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-middleton">Frederick Middleton's</a> North-West Field Force won at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/batoche">Batoche</a> in May 1885. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-riel">Riel</a> surrendered and was hanged in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/regina-saskatchewan">Regina</a> that November, and eight <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cree">Cree</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assiniboine">Assiniboine</a> men were hanged at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battleford">Battleford</a>. The execution deeply divided English and French <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/canada">Canada</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/provisional-government-of-saskatchewan.jpg" alt="Provisional Government of Saskatchewan" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Hstoops · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flagoftheprovisionalgovernmentofsask.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1885 CE – 1885 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Batoche</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Louis Riel, Gabriel Dumont</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Roman Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>French, Michif, Cree</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/canada">Canada</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Exovedate</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1885&amp;focus=provisional-government-of-saskatchewan" aria-label="Provisional Government of Saskatchewan on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2304 359 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Provisional Government of Saskatchewan lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M2624 615L3203 831"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M3203 831h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M2624 615h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M2624 615h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Batoche. <a href="/atlas?year=1885&amp;focus=provisional-government-of-saskatchewan">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

